Seeing the earlier posts, I can only make these suggestions,
A combination of the below:


1. learn force bolt (identifying a spellbooks level is easy in a shop)

2. concentrate on building up your strength, weapon skill and weapon
enchantment *before* sokoban. You should know how much remove curse,
identify, enchant armor and enchant weapon cost, so iding those four
should be easy. 

3. It's better to have bad luck and be alive than to have good luck and
be dead. 

4. You know what sort of nonsence to expect in sokoban, so have
telepathy and an uncursed blindfold before you go there (along with a
pickaxe and some sort of range weapon/spell/wand.) Sleep and magic
missile are *very* good and are low level. 

5. Build up your armor class as much as possible. You should have zero
to -5 at a minimum before doing sokoban lower if you haven't any
healing/regeneration. 



